# Used by `npm run build`.
#
# "/api" means "the same server that served this page". That works when the
# Python backend serves the built frontend, which is how it runs today.
#
# If you later host the frontend somewhere separate (Vercel, Netlify), set
# VITE_API_URL there to the full backend URL, for example
#   https://your-api.onrender.com/api
# A value set in the hosting dashboard overrides this file.
VITE_API_URL=/api
